
 •  In Java, the computeIfAbsent() method of the HashMap class is used to compute and insert a value for a specific key to a HashMap
    only if the key does not already have a value.

 map.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> value);
    ➼ If key is absent:
         create value
         put into map
         return value

    ➼ Else:
        return existing value